irit with  various religious objects  after witnessing no reaction they  determined that he is not possessed  this raises some huge questions how does  this demon seem to come and go  as it pleases as lorraine later states  demons don't just disappear  so this forces the warrens to retrace  their steps and circle back to the  glacial house  david glatzel's very first demonic  encounter took place  in the guest room where he was attacked  by a dark spirit lurking within the  waterbed  after ed observes rotted wood on the  floor that doesn't appear to be from  water damage  lorraine makes her way under the house  and discovers a gooey black substance  dripping from the ceiling as well as a  unique type of witch's totem derived  from animal bones  in surprise surprise it's positioned  directly under the guest room  we then learn that this particular totem  is often used by master satanists to  inflict a three-phase curse on someone  in phase one a demon is summoned in  phase 2 the possessed individual takes a  life  finally in phase 3 the demon departs all  of this explains why arnie was able to  read from the bible without exhibiting  any demonic reactions  but it also raises the crucial question  of who made and placed all these totems  in the house the warrens receive a tip  about a priest who's an expert  on the occult and satanic rituals his  name is father krasner and much like the  warrens  he has a chamber of demonic relics of  his own  after seeing a photo of the totem  discovered under the glatzel residence  he knows exactly who the warrens are up  against the totem is commonly used by a  cult  known as the disciples of the ram a fun  nod that conjuring universe enthusiasts  will recognize as the name of the same  cult from the annabelle movies  krasner warns the warrens that these  sophisticated satanists  aren't adversaries to be taken lightly  as we discover later in the film the  mystery occultist pulling all the  strings is indeed the god-faced woman  we saw earlier lola who also happens to  be krasner's very  own estranged daughter who he raised and  kept in secret from the priesthood  at a young age lola took up some of her  father's  interests and developed a dark obsession  for witchcraft and the occult  she's been operating within the tunnels  beneath his farmhouse  the entire time when the warrens first  questioned krasner about the satanist's  rituals  and asked why they'd target a little boy  earlier in the movie  he shrugs it off explaining why is  irrelevant  he claims that there is no method to the  madness the satanists are simply  organizers of chaos who worship the  devil and offer him blood sacrifices at  random  as we come to find out later his  explanation made an effort to conceal  the involvement and identity of his  daughter  during the third act when he finally  confesses to lorraine that his daughter  has been the mastermind behind these  curses we finally discover the meaning  of her grand scheme drew the trustee  sidekick of the warrens discovers a  latin language passage within the pages  of an ancient book of witchcraft the  scripture talks of a curse that says the  inflicted  must kill someone then kill themselves  once the curse is started  it must be completed at all costs lola's  soul depends on it  since drew's latin is a bit rusty  lorraine opts to take the book to  krasner for a full translation  as krasner deciphers the latin passages  it is discovered that three sacrifices  are required for lola to complete the  ritual  purity love and faith or the child the  lover  and finally the man of god which  explains the three  totems that are in play the first is the  one found under the glatzel house  which ultimately inflicted arnie the  lover the second was discovered by  detectives in danvers massachusetts who  stumbled upon the totem while piecing  together the murder of katie lincoln  and the missing prime suspect her own  best friend jessica louise strong  the child and as you may 